IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- PART VI: SUBSIDIARY LEGISLATION (ss 40 to 47).
-- Section 41(1)(b) and (2), the commencement of subsidiary legislation, are in wa-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Most of Part VI describes what a power to make subsidiary legislation includes, which matters to the person
-- who is subject to the legislation as: what can be made binding on them, and when it stops.

§ `Part VI -- Subsidiary legislation`

§§ `40. Governor to make subsidiary legislation`

-- Section 40: if a written law provides that subsidiary legislation may or shall be made and does not provide by whom,
-- it shall be made by the Governor.  If no written law provides for subsidiary legislation, the section does not apply.
-- src:468 | If a written law provides that subsidiary legislation may or shall be made and does not provide by whom such subsidiary legislation may or shall be made, any subsidiary legislation made under such a provision shall be made by the Governor.
@ref s 40 (src:468)
GIVEN `a written law provides that subsidiary legislation may or shall be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written law says who makes it, if it does` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`who makes the subsidiary legislation` `a written law provides that subsidiary legislation may or shall be made` `the written law says who makes it, if it does` MEANS
    IF `a written law provides that subsidiary legislation may or shall be made`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the written law says who makes it, if it does`
        WHEN JUST someone THEN JUST someone
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST "the Governor"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `41. Publication and commencement of subsidiary legislation`

-- Section 41(1)(a): subsidiary legislation made under a power in a written law is published in the Gazette or on the
-- WA legislation website.  (Section 41(1)(b) and (2) are in wa-interpretation-time.l4.)
-- src:471 | (a) be published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website; and
@ref s 41(1)(a) (src:471)
GIVEN `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published on the WA legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary legislation is published as section 41(1)(a) requires` `it is published in the Gazette` `it is published on the WA legislation website` MEANS
    `it is published in the Gazette` OR `it is published on the WA legislation website`

§§ `42. Laying regulations, rules, local laws and bylaws before Parliament, and disallowance`

-- Sitting days are a fact about a House: the caller lists the dates on which the House actually sat (s 5 "sitting
-- days"), earliest first, across sessions and Parliaments (s 42(3)).

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the nth of the dates` n days MEANS
    CONSIDER days
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF n EQUALS 1 THEN JUST d ELSE `the nth of the dates` (n MINUS 1) rest

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the sitting days after the day` day days MEANS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD Day d GREATER THAN Day day) days

-- Section 42(1): all regulations shall be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House next following
-- publication of the regulations in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website.  Taken as: the 6th sitting day after
-- the day of publication (the publication day is excluded, s 61(1)(b), "after").  If fewer than 6 sitting days are
-- listed, the last day is not yet known (NOTHING).
-- src:476 | (1) All regulations shall be laid before each House of Parliament within 6 sitting days of such House next following publication of the regulations in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website.
@ref s 42(1) (src:476)
GIVEN `the day the regulations are published` IS A DATE
      `the sitting days of the House, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for laying the regulations before the House` `the day the regulations are published` `the sitting days of the House, earliest first` MEANS
    `the nth of the dates` 6 (`the sitting days after the day` `the day the regulations are published` `the sitting days of the House, earliest first`)

-- Section 42(2), first limb: if either House passes a resolution disallowing regulations, notice of which has been
-- given within 14 sitting days of that House after the regulations were laid before it, the regulations cease to have
-- effect.  The last day for the notice is the 14th sitting day after the day they were laid.  Subsection (3) says
-- the "period of 14 days" where (2) says 14 sitting days; the text of (2) is encoded as written (fork F12 in NOTES.md).
-- src:477 | (2) Notwithstanding any provision in any Act to the contrary, if either House of Parliament passes a resolution disallowing any regulations of which resolution notice has been given within 14 sitting days of such House after such regulations have been laid before it or if any regulations are not laid before both Houses of Parliament in accordance with subsection (1), such regulations shall thereupon cease to have effect, but without affecting the validity or curing the invalidity of anything done or of the omission of anything in the meantime.
-- src:478 | (3) Subsection (2) applies notwithstanding that the period of 14 days referred to in that subsection, or part of that period, does not occur in the same session of Parliament or during the same Parliament as that in which the regulations are laid before the House concerned.
@ref s 42(2) (src:477)
@ref s 42(3) (src:478)
GIVEN `the day the regulations were laid before the House` IS A DATE
      `the sitting days of the House, earliest first` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for giving notice of a resolution disallowing the regulations` `the day the regulations were laid before the House` `the sitting days of the House, earliest first` MEANS
    `the nth of the dates` 14 (`the sitting days after the day` `the day the regulations were laid before the House` `the sitting days of the House, earliest first`)

-- Section 42(2): the regulations thereupon cease to have effect if (i) either House passes a resolution
-- disallowing them of which notice was given within the 14 sitting days, or (ii) they are not laid before both Houses
-- in accordance with subsection (1).
@ref s 42(2) (src:477)
GIVEN `a House passed a resolution disallowing them, notice of which was given within 14 sitting days after they were laid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were not laid before both Houses in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the regulations cease to have effect` `a House passed a resolution disallowing them, notice of which was given within 14 sitting days after they were laid` `they were not laid before both Houses in accordance with subsection (1)` MEANS
        `a House passed a resolution disallowing them, notice of which was given within 14 sitting days after they were laid`
    OR  `they were not laid before both Houses in accordance with subsection (1)`

-- Section 42(2), closing words: the regulations cease to have effect without affecting the validity, or curing the
-- invalidity, of anything done, or of the omission of anything, in the meantime.
@ref s 42(2) (src:477)
GIVEN `the thing done in the meantime was valid when done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the thing done in the meantime is valid after the regulations cease to have effect` `the thing done in the meantime was valid when done` MEANS
    `the thing done in the meantime was valid when done`

-- Section 42(4): if both Houses pass a resolution amending the regulations or substituting other regulations for
-- those disallowed, the amended or substituted regulations take effect after the expiration of 7 days from the
-- publication of the notice provided for in (5).  The publication day is excluded ("from", s 61(1)(b)), so the 7 days
-- are the 7 days after it; "after the expiration" of them is the next day, which is the 8th day after publication
-- (fork F5 in NOTES.md; the day begins the operation of the law, s 21).
-- src:479 | (4) Notwithstanding any provision in any Act to the contrary, if both Houses of Parliament at any time pass a resolution originating in either House amending any such regulations or substituting other regulations for that which has been disallowed by either House under subsection (2), then on the passing of any such resolution —
-- src:480 | (a) amending regulations, the regulations so amended shall, after the expiration of 7 days from the publication in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website of the notice provided for in subsection (5), take effect as so amended;
-- src:481 | (b) substituting regulations in place of regulations disallowed, the regulations so substituted shall, after the expiration of 7 days from the publication in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website of the notice provided for in subsection (5), take effect in place of that for which the regulations are so substituted.
@ref s 42(4) (src:479-481)
GIVEN `the day the notice of the resolution is published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day the amended or substituted regulations take effect` `the day the notice of the resolution is published` MEANS
    `the day the notice of the resolution is published` PLUS 8

-- Section 42(5): when a resolution has been passed under (2) or (4), notice of it shall be published in the Gazette
-- or on the WA legislation website within 21 days of the passing.  "Of" is read like "from" (fork F6): the day of
-- passing is excluded, so the 21st day after it is the last day.
-- src:482 | (5) When a resolution has been passed under subsection (2) or (4), notice of such resolution shall be published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website within 21 days of the passing of the resolution.
@ref s 42(5) (src:482)
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for publishing notice of the resolution` `the day the resolution was passed` MEANS
    `the day the resolution was passed` PLUS 21

DECLARE `How regulations came to an end under section 42` IS ONE OF
    `disallowed by a resolution`
    `not laid in accordance with subsection (1)`

-- Section 42(6): notwithstanding s 37(1), where (a) regulations are disallowed under s 42 or are not laid before both
-- Houses in accordance with (1), and (b) they amended or repealed regulations that were in operation immediately before
-- they came into operation, the disallowance or the failure revives the previous regulations on and after the day of
-- the disallowance or, in the case of failure to comply with (1), on and after the day next following the last day for
-- compliance with (1).
-- src:483 | (6) Notwithstanding section 37(1), where —
-- src:484 | (a) regulations are disallowed under this section or are not laid before both Houses of Parliament in accordance with subsection (1); and
-- src:485 | (b) those regulations amended or repealed regulations that were in operation immediately before the firstmentioned regulations came into operation,
-- src:486 | the disallowance or failure to comply with subsection (1) revives the previous regulations on and after the day of the disallowance or, in the case of failure to comply with subsection (1), on and after the day next following the last day for compliance with subsection (1).
@ref s 42(6) (src:483-486)
GIVEN how IS A `How regulations came to an end under section 42`
      `they amended or repealed regulations in operation immediately before they came into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the disallowance` IS A DATE
      `the last day for compliance with subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day the previous regulations are revived` how `they amended or repealed regulations in operation immediately before they came into operation` `the day of the disallowance` `the last day for compliance with subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `they amended or repealed regulations in operation immediately before they came into operation`
    THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `disallowed by a resolution` THEN JUST `the day of the disallowance`
        WHEN `not laid in accordance with subsection (1)` THEN JUST (`the last day for compliance with subsection (1)` PLUS 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 42(7): if a written law empowers or directs the making of regulations by a person other than the Governor
-- and requires that they be confirmed or approved by the Governor or another person or authority before having the
-- force of law, subsection (1) does not apply to them unless they have been confirmed or approved as so required.
-- src:487 | (7) If a written law empowers or directs the making of regulations by a person other than the Governor and requires that the regulations be confirmed or approved by the Governor or by any other person or authority before having the force of law, subsection (1) does not apply to such regulations unless they have been confirmed or approved as so required.
@ref s 42(7) (src:487)
GIVEN `they are made by a person other than the Governor and must be confirmed or approved before having the force of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have been confirmed or approved as required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection (1) applies to the regulations` `they are made by a person other than the Governor and must be confirmed or approved before having the force of law` `they have been confirmed or approved as required` MEANS
        (NOT `they are made by a person other than the Governor and must be confirmed or approved before having the force of law`)
    OR  `they have been confirmed or approved as required`

DECLARE `Instrument a reference to regulations might be about` IS ONE OF
    `regulations`
    `a regulation`
    `part of a regulation`
    `rules`
    `local laws`
    `bylaws`
    `some other kind of subsidiary legislation`

-- Section 42(8): in s 42 a reference to regulations includes a regulation or part of a regulation, and regulations
-- includes rules, local laws and bylaws.
-- src:488 | (8) In this section —
-- src:489 | (a) a reference to regulations shall be construed as including a reference to a regulation or part of a regulation; and
-- src:490 | (b) regulations includes rules, local laws and bylaws.
@ref s 42(8) (src:488-490)
GIVEN x IS A `Instrument a reference to regulations might be about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 42 treats it as regulations` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `some other kind of subsidiary legislation` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `43. Power to make subsidiary legislation, general provisions about`

-- Section 43(1): subsidiary legislation shall not be inconsistent with the written law under which it is made, or
-- with any Act, and is void to the extent of any inconsistency.
-- src:493 | (1) Subsidiary legislation shall not be inconsistent with the provisions of the written law under which it is made, or of any Act, and subsidiary legislation shall be void to the extent of any such inconsistency.
@ref s 43(1) (src:493)
GIVEN `it is inconsistent with the written law under which it is made, or with any Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary legislation is void to the extent of the inconsistency` `it is inconsistent with the written law under which it is made, or with any Act` MEANS
    `it is inconsistent with the written law under which it is made, or with any Act`

-- Section 43(2): subsidiary legislation that purports to be made in exercise of a particular power or powers is deemed
-- also made in exercise of all powers under which it may be made.
-- src:494 | (2) Where any subsidiary legislation purports to be made in exercise of a particular power or powers, it shall be deemed also to be made in exercise of all powers under which it may be made.
@ref s 43(2) (src:494)
GIVEN `it may be made under that power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it purports to be made under another power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is deemed to be made in exercise of the power` `it may be made under that power` `it purports to be made under another power` MEANS
    `it may be made under that power`

-- Section 43(3): it is presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, that all conditions and preliminary steps
-- precedent to making subsidiary legislation have been complied with and performed.  With evidence to the contrary
-- the presumption gives no answer (NOTHING).
-- src:495 | (3) It shall be presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, that all conditions and preliminary steps precedent to the making of subsidiary legislation have been complied with and performed.
@ref s 43(3) (src:495)
GIVEN `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`all conditions and preliminary steps precedent to making it are presumed complied with` `there is evidence to the contrary` MEANS
    IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Section 43(4): a power to make subsidiary legislation includes a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to
-- the like conditions, to amend or repeal it.
-- src:496 | (4) Where a written law confers a power to make subsidiary legislation, it shall be deemed also to include a power exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like conditions (if any) to amend or repeal any such subsidiary legislation.
@ref s 43(4) (src:496)
GIVEN `a written law confers a power to make subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the power includes a power to amend or repeal the subsidiary legislation, in the like manner and on the like conditions` `a written law confers a power to make subsidiary legislation` MEANS
    `a written law confers a power to make subsidiary legislation`

-- Section 43(5): where the power is for a general purpose and also for special purposes incidental to it, the
-- enumeration of the special purposes does not derogate from the generality of the power for the general purpose.
-- src:497 | (5) Where a written law confers power on a person to make subsidiary legislation for any general purpose and also for any special purposes incidental thereto, the enumeration of the special purposes shall not derogate from the generality of the powers conferred with reference to the general purpose.
@ref s 43(5) (src:497)
GIVEN `the special purposes are listed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the listing of special purposes limits the power for the general purpose` `the special purposes are listed` MEANS FALSE

-- Section 43(6): subject to s 3(3), regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws made under a power conferred by an
-- enactment passed after the commencement of this Act may provide that contravention of a provision constitutes an
-- offence and may provide for a penalty not exceeding a fine of $1 000.  For an enactment not passed after the
-- commencement (as s 3(3) reads that), the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:498 | (6) Subject to section 3(3), regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws made under a power conferred by an enactment passed after the commencement of this Act may provide that contravention of a provision thereof constitutes an offence and may provide for a penalty in respect of such a contravention not exceeding a fine of $1 000.
@ref s 43(6) (src:498)
GIVEN `the day the enactment conferring the power was passed` IS A DATE
      `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` `the day the enactment conferring the power was passed` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` MEANS
    IF `counts as passed or made after the commencement for ss 17, 25, 43(6), 50 and 64` `the day the enactment conferring the power was passed` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law`
    THEN JUST 1000
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 43(6) (src:498)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      `the day the enactment conferring the power was passed` IS A DATE
      `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a fine is within the limit section 43(6) allows` fine `the day the enactment conferring the power was passed` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` `the day the enactment conferring the power was passed` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST (fine AT MOST limit)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Way a power to make subsidiary legislation may be exercised` IS ONE OF
    `in relation to all cases to which the power extends`
    `in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions`
    `in relation to a specified case or class of case`
    `the same provision for all cases`
    `different provision for different cases or classes of case`
    `different provisions for the same case or class of case for different purposes`
    `unconditionally`
    `subject to a specified condition`
    `to apply at all times or at a specified time`
    `to apply throughout the State or in a specified part of it`
    `to require a matter to be in accordance with a specified standard or requirement`
    `to require a matter to be approved by or to the satisfaction of a specified person or body or class`
    `to confer a discretionary authority on a specified person or body or class`
    `to exempt persons or things or a class, unconditionally or on conditions, wholly or to a specified extent`
    `in some way not listed`

-- Section 43(7), (8) and (9): a power to make subsidiary legislation may be exercised in any of the ways listed
-- ("specified" means specified in the subsidiary legislation).  A way not listed is not dealt with (NOTHING).
-- src:499 | (7) A power to make subsidiary legislation may be exercised —
-- src:500 | (a) either in relation to all cases to which the power extends, or in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions, or in relation to any specified case or class of case; and
-- src:501 | (b) so as to make, as respects the cases in relation to which it is exercised —
-- src:502 | (i) the same provision for all cases in relation to which the power is exercised, or different provision for different cases or classes of case, or different provisions for the same case or class of case for different purposes of the legislation; or
-- src:503 | (ii) any such provision either unconditionally or subject to any specified condition.
-- src:504 | (8) Subsidiary legislation may be made —
-- src:505 | (a) so as to apply —
-- src:506 | (i) at all times or at a specified time;
-- src:507 | (ii) throughout the State or in a specified part of the State;
-- src:508 | and
-- src:509 | (b) so as to require a matter affected by the legislation to be —
-- src:510 | (i) in accordance with a specified standard or specified requirement;
-- src:511 | (ii) approved by or to the satisfaction of a specified person or body or a specified class of person or body;
-- src:512 | and
-- src:513 | (c) so as to confer a discretionary authority on a specified person or body or a specified class of person or body; and
-- src:514 | (d) so as to provide, in a specified case or class of case for the exemption of persons or things or a class of persons or things from the provisions of the subsidiary legislation, whether unconditionally or on specified conditions or conditions additionally imposed and either wholly or to such an extent as is specified or otherwise determined.
-- src:515 | (9) In subsections (7) and (8) specified means specified in the subsidiary legislation.
@ref s 43(7) (src:499-503)
@ref s 43(8) (src:504-514)
@ref s 43(9) (src:515)
GIVEN x IS A `Way a power to make subsidiary legislation may be exercised`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `in some way not listed` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 43(9): in subsections (7) and (8), "specified" means specified in the subsidiary legislation.
-- src:515 | (9) In subsections (7) and (8) specified means specified in the subsidiary legislation.
@ref s 43(9) (src:515)
GIVEN `it is specified in the subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is specified for section 43(7) and (8)` `it is specified in the subsidiary legislation` MEANS
    `it is specified in the subsidiary legislation`

§§ `44. Words and expressions in subsidiary legislation, meaning of`

-- Section 44(1): words and expressions used in subsidiary legislation have the same respective meanings as in the
-- written law under which it is made.  Section 44(2): a reference in subsidiary legislation to the Act is a reference
-- to the Act under which it is made.
-- src:518 | (1) Words and expressions used in subsidiary legislation shall have the same respective meanings as in the written law under which the subsidiary legislation is made.
-- src:519 | (2) A reference in subsidiary legislation to the Act shall be construed as a reference to the Act under which the subsidiary legislation is made.
@ref s 44(1) (src:518)
@ref s 44(2) (src:519)
GIVEN `the Act under which the subsidiary legislation is made` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the Act a reference in subsidiary legislation to the Act means` `the Act under which the subsidiary legislation is made` MEANS
    `the Act under which the subsidiary legislation is made`

@ref s 44(1) (src:518)
GIVEN `the word is used in the subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the word has the same meaning as in the written law under which the subsidiary legislation is made` `the word is used in the subsidiary legislation` MEANS
    `the word is used in the subsidiary legislation`

§§ `45. Fees and charges`

DECLARE `Provision about fees or charges` IS ONE OF
    `specific fees or charges`
    `maximum or minimum fees or charges`
    `maximum and minimum fees or charges`
    `ad valorem fees or charges`
    `payment generally or under specified conditions or in specified circumstances`
    `reduction, waiver or refund, in whole or in part`
    `some other provision about fees or charges`

DECLARE `Way a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` IS ONE OF
    `in respect of certain matters or transactions or classes of them`
    `in respect of certain documents or classes of document`
    `when any event happens or ceases to happen`
    `in respect of certain persons or classes of person`
    `in respect of any combination of those`
    `subject to conditions specified in the subsidiary legislation or in the discretion of a person it specifies`
    `in some other way`

-- Section 45(1): where subsidiary legislation makes provision in respect of fees or charges, it may provide for all or
-- any of (a) to (f).  Section 45(3) is shown as deleted.
-- src:521 | (1) Where provision is made by subsidiary legislation in respect of fees or charges, the subsidiary legislation may provide for all or any of the following matters —
-- src:522 | (a) specific fees or charges; and
-- src:523 | (b) maximum or minimum fees or charges; and
-- src:524 | (c) maximum and minimum fees or charges; and
-- src:525 | (d) ad valorem fees or charges; and
-- src:526 | (e) the payment of fees and charges either generally or under specified conditions or in specified circumstances; and
-- src:527 | (f) the reduction, waiver or refund, in whole or in part, of such fees or charges.
@ref s 45(1) (src:521-527)
GIVEN x IS A `Provision about fees or charges`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsidiary legislation may provide for` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `some other provision about fees or charges` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 45(2): a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply generally or specifically in the ways listed (a) to
-- (e), and subject to conditions specified or in the discretion of a person specified.
-- src:528 | (2) Where any reduction, waiver or refund, in whole or in part, of any fee or charge is provided for by subsidiary legislation, such reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply or be applicable either generally or specifically —
-- src:529 | (a) in respect of certain matters or transactions or classes of matter or transaction; or
-- src:530 | (b) in respect of certain documents or classes of document; or
-- src:531 | (c) when any event happens or ceases to happen; or
-- src:532 | (d) in respect of certain persons or classes of person; or
-- src:533 | (e) in respect of any combination of such matters, transactions, documents, events, or persons,
-- src:534 | and may be expressed to apply or to be applicable subject to such conditions as may be specified in the subsidiary legislation or in the discretion of any person specified in the subsidiary legislation.
@ref s 45(2) (src:528-534)
GIVEN x IS A `Way a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reduction, waiver or refund may be expressed to apply` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `in some other way` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `45A. Fees for licences, effect of power to prescribe`

DECLARE `Expenditure asked about under section 45A` IS ONE OF
    `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in the establishment or administration of the scheme or system under which the licence is issued`
    `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in respect of matters to which the licence relates`
    `any other expenditure`

DECLARE `Fee asked about under section 45A` IS ONE OF
    `a fee for a licence`
    `a fee for, or in relation to, the issue of a licence`
    `a fee payable on an application for the issue of a licence`
    `some other fee`

-- Section 45A(2): expenditure is not relevant to s 45A(1) unless it has been or is to be incurred (a) in the
-- establishment or administration of the scheme or system under which the licence is issued, or (b) in respect of
-- matters to which the licence relates.
-- src:539 | (2) Expenditure is not relevant for the purposes of subsection (1) unless it has been or is to be incurred —
-- src:540 | (a) in the establishment or administration of the scheme or system under which the licence is issued; or
-- src:541 | (b) in respect of matters to which the licence relates.
@ref s 45A(2) (src:539-541)
GIVEN x IS A `Expenditure asked about under section 45A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`expenditure is relevant to the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in the establishment or administration of the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `expenditure incurred or to be incurred in respect of matters to which the licence relates` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other expenditure` THEN FALSE

-- Section 45A(1) and (3): a power conferred by a written law to prescribe or impose a fee for a licence includes power
-- to prescribe or impose a fee that will allow recovery of expenditure that is relevant to the scheme or system under
-- which the licence is issued; a fee for a licence includes a fee for, or in relation to, the issue of a licence and a
-- fee payable on an application for the issue of a licence.  Other fees are not dealt with (NOTHING).
-- src:538 | (1) A power conferred by a written law to prescribe or impose a fee for a licence includes power to prescribe or impose a fee that will allow recovery of expenditure that is relevant to the scheme or system under which the licence is issued.
-- src:542 | (3) The reference in subsection (1) to a fee for a licence includes reference to a fee for, or in relation to, the issue of a licence and a fee payable on an application for the issue of a licence.
@ref s 45A(1) (src:538)
@ref s 45A(3) (src:542)
GIVEN fee IS A `Fee asked about under section 45A`
      x IS A `Expenditure asked about under section 45A`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a power to prescribe a fee allows it to recover the expenditure` fee x MEANS
    CONSIDER fee
    WHEN `some other fee` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (`expenditure is relevant to the scheme or system under which the licence is issued` x)

DECLARE `Thing named in section 45A(4)` IS ONE OF
    `a charge, for the word fee`
    `to grant, give or renew, for the word issue`
    `a registration, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption, for the word licence`
    `to grant, for the word issue`
    `to give, for the word issue`
    `to renew, for the word issue`
    `a registration, for the word licence`
    `a right, for the word licence`
    `a permit, for the word licence`
    `an authority, for the word licence`
    `an approval, for the word licence`
    `an exemption, for the word licence`
    `something else`

-- Section 45A(4): in this section fee includes charge; issue includes grant, give or renew; licence includes
-- registration, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption.
-- The printed list for issue and the printed list for licence are each a constructor above, and so is each constituent of
-- those lists, so a question about "permit" alone or "renew" alone is answered.  "fee includes charge" has one constituent.
-- src:543 | (4) In this section —
-- src:544 | fee includes charge;
-- src:545 | issue includes grant, give or renew;
-- src:546 | licence includes registration, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption.
@ref s 45A(4) (src:543-546)
GIVEN x IS A `Thing named in section 45A(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `46. Reference to written law includes reference to subsidiary legislation made under it`

DECLARE `What a reference to a written law is about` IS ONE OF
    `a written law`
    `this Act, as referred to in an Act`
    `an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act`
    `something that is not a written law, an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act`

-- Section 46(1), (1a), (2): a reference in a written law to a written law is construed to include subsidiary legislation
-- made under it (for example, "this Act" in an Act includes subsidiary legislation made under the Act); a reference to
-- an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act includes subsidiary legislation made under that Act.
-- src:549 | (1) A reference in a written law to a written law shall be construed so as to include a reference to any subsidiary legislation made under that written law.
-- src:550 | (1a) An example of the operation of subsection (1) is that a reference in an Act to “this Act” includes a reference to any subsidiary legislation made under the Act.
-- src:551 | (2) A reference in a written law to an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act shall be construed so as to include a reference to any subsidiary legislation made under that Act.
@ref s 46(1) (src:549)
@ref s 46(1a) (src:550)
@ref s 46(2) (src:551)
GIVEN x IS A `What a reference to a written law is about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under it` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `something that is not a written law, an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `47. Acts done under subsidiary legislation deemed done under Act`

-- Section 47: any act done under subsidiary legislation is deemed to be done under the written law under which the
-- subsidiary legislation was made.
-- src:554 | Any act done under subsidiary legislation shall be deemed to be done under the written law under which the subsidiary legislation was made.
@ref s 47 (src:554)
GIVEN `the act is done under subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the act is deemed done under the written law under which the subsidiary legislation was made` `the act is done under subsidiary legislation` MEANS
    `the act is done under subsidiary legislation`
